1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:04,240
While the golden Lanka is considered a symbol of Ravan's ego,

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,160
many believe that its true creator was Mahadev himself.

3
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:13,693
This story is often heard,

4
00:00:13,693 --> 00:00:16,280
but we found no basis for it in any scripture.

5
00:00:18,430 --> 00:00:19,854
First hear the story.

6
00:00:19,854 --> 00:00:22,770
The story says at Mata Parvati's insistence

7
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,480
Mahadev built a divine golden city in the midst of the ocean.

8
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,903
When the housewarming ritual was completed,

9
00:00:29,903 --> 00:00:30,790
Shiva thundered.

10
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:33,517
Ask, Rishi Vishrava,

11
00:00:33,517 --> 00:00:38,180
today no wealth of the three worlds will stand in your way as your donation.

12
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:42,720
The sage's inner greed awoke. He said,

13
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:45,609
[Vishrava] O Augharddani,

14
00:00:45,609 --> 00:00:48,160
please give me this golden city as a gift.

15
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,890
Mata Parvati was stunned,

16
00:00:50,890 --> 00:00:52,220
but Mahadev smiled.

17
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:54,250
[Shiva] So be it.

18
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:55,923
What Shiva gives,

19
00:00:55,923 --> 00:00:57,510
he does not look upon again.

20
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:00,950
An angered Parvati cursed him,

21
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:05,960
[Parvati] This very gold will become the cause of the destruction of your lineage.

22
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:07,760
And that is what happened.

23
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:11,967
Mahadev proved that he is the master of wealth,

24
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:14,220
not its slave. Har Har Mahadev.

25
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:16,110
So did this really happen?

26
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:18,450
Let us see in the next story,

27
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,230
what is written in the Valmiki Ramayan?

28
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:23,708
To make sure the next story reaches you,

29
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,720
follow or subscribe to Naad Katha.

